        "sys_immortal_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Lang Ya land spirit uses the blade path killer move Slaughtering Immortal Guillotine in a fight, and the narration names it among successive path killer moves.",
      "chapters": [
        880
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "what-the-path-governs",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_lang_ya_land_spirit",
        "move_slaughtering_immortal_guillotine"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In a Late Antiquity Era river segment, Lord Huang Shi feels a strong sword path and blade path aura. He recalls the blade path demonic immortal Dao Jiu Lang, whose fight with the sword path expert Xi Yuan left a blade river segment filled with sword qi and blade light.",
      "chapters": [
        1432
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "what-the-path-governs",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "evt_era_late",
        "char_huang_shi",
        "char_dao_jiu_lang",
        "char_xi_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Blade path is an extremely small path beside paths such as metal path, fire path, and earth path. Sword path cannot be left out when mentioning blade path: the two are deeply interconnected and yet conflicting, because both originate from edge Gu. Edge Gu appears in The Legends of Ren Zu, and autumn blade plain is full of blade path dao marks that form countless wild edge Gu naturally. Meng Tu is a rank seven Gu Immortal who cultivates blade path at peak rank seven battle strength. His blade path sits at quasi-great grandmaster, and he stays on autumn blade plain seeking a breakthrough by imitating Ren Zu’s actions.",
      "chapters": [
        1563
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "edge-gu-and-autumn-blade-plain",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "path_sword",
        "gu_edge_immortal_gu",
        "sys_the_legends_of_ren_zu",
        "char_meng_tribe_meng_tu",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "char_ren_zu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan identifies bladewing Immortal Gu as Meng Tu’s blade path Immortal Gu: a white butterfly the size of a fist. After Meng Tu’s self-detonation, his blade path dao marks are engraved into autumn blade plain.",
      "chapters": [
        1565
      ],
